From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 per-run random isolated world names

Security audit RC-500 F-16. Bridge 0.66.0. An extension's content-script world
takes the extension's name, and Runtime.addBinding with executionContextName
binds every context of that name, so an extension named rearc.host got
rearcLinkPeek and one named rearc.boost.<id> got __rearcPostJSON. ReArc's
world names now carry a 128-bit random token chosen once per run, unknown to
pages and extensions.

Last rebased: 2026-11-10 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.96 (2ad9b7f5a8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

